course: dictionary
lesson: 6339
title: Words for loss
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words hold a big feeling in just one word. «Mourning» is one of them. It means great sadness shown after someone dies. The words around it give you clues to its meaning.
explain: «Americans celebrate Thanksgiving every November, and for many Native people it is also a day of mourning for what followed.» The word «also» tells you the day means something different to them. Mourning must be a feeling of deep sadness, because the sentence sets it against celebrating.
explain: You may see «in mourning», as in a family «in mourning» for their grandad. This means they are grieving and showing sadness after a death. Mourning can also be the time when people show this sadness, often with special customs or black clothes.
explain: Mourn is a verb, so mourning can be its -ing form too. «They are mourning their grandad» means they are feeling and showing sadness right now. Ask yourself: is it a feeling, a time, or an action?
fact: «Mourning» means great sadness shown after someone dies.
fact: A «day of mourning» is a day when people show their sadness, often with special customs.
fact: Some cultures wear black or white clothes for mourning.
fact: «In mourning» means grieving for someone who has died.
fact: «Mourn» is the verb: to mourn means to feel and show deep sadness after a death.
exercise: «Americans celebrate Thanksgiving every November, and for many Native people it is also a day of mourning for what followed.» What does mourning mean here? | A long journey by train | A happy party with lots of food | A small, quiet walk in the park | *Great sadness shown after something terrible
exercise: Which word is the -ing form of mourn? | *mourning | moaning | morning
exercise: A family is «in mourning». What does this tell you? | They are very hungry | They are going on holiday | *They are grieving after a death | They are cooking a big feast
test: What is a day of mourning? | A cold, rainy day at the seaside | A happy day with music and games | A day when the shops are closed for a sale | *A day when people show deep sadness after a death
test: What does the verb mourn mean? | To laugh loudly at a joke | To move quickly through a crowd | To find something lost under a sofa | *To feel and show deep sadness after a death
exam: Which sentence uses mourning as a noun? | We went mourning on the hill after school | They are mourning their grandad today | *The country held a national day of mourning | Mourning the lost puppy, she searched all day
